<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Keonjhar State</h1><p class="st-meta">1128 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Keonjhargarh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Bhanja dynasty state in the forested hills of northern Odisha, known for the Bhuyan risings of 1868 and 1891 against its Raja.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tradition holds that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kendujhar">Keonjhar</a> was founded in the 12th century by a younger brother of the ruler of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mayurbhanj-state">Mayurbhanj</a>, so that both states were ruled by branches of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhanja-dynasty">Bhanja dynasty</a>. The capital was Keonjhargarh.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kendujhar">Keonjhar</a> was hilly and wooded, with a large population of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhuyan">Bhuyan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juang">Juang peoples</a>, whose obligations to the Raja caused tension. Disputed successions and harsh exactions led to Bhuyan revolts in 1868 and 1891, the second led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dharanidhar-naik">Dharanidhar Naik</a>, both suppressed with British help. The state was later known for its iron ore.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kendujhar">Keonjhar</a> merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a> on 1 January 1948 and is now a district of Odisha.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/keonjhar-state.jpg" alt="Keonjhar State" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: Xufanc · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Keonjharflag1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1128 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Keonjhargarh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Odia</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Keonjhar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1538&amp;focus=keonjhar-state" aria-label="Keonjhar State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6870 1378 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Keonjhar State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7190 1634L7364 1601M7190 1634L7364 1602M7190 1634L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7190 1634h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7190 1634h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1538&amp;focus=keonjhar-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
